.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt DELL1320C 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dell1320c
.Nd set up and manage print queues for the Dell Color Laser 1320c
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm add
.Ar address | uri
.Op Fl \-name Ar name
.Op Fl \-description Ar text
.Op Fl \-location Ar text
.Op Fl \-paper Ar size
.Op Fl \-protocol Cm lpd | socket
.Op Fl \-default
.Op Fl \-shared
.Nm
.Cm remove
.Op Ar name
.Nm
.Cm trays
.Ar address
.Nm
.Cm list
.Nm
.Cm refresh
.Nm
.Cm uninstall
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
creates and manages CUPS print queues that use the
Dell Color Laser 1320c driver.
Commands that change printer settings must be run as root, for example with
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Bl -tag -width uninstall
.It Cm add
Creates a print queue for the printer at
.Ar address ,
or updates the queue if it already exists.
An address is a host name, an IPv4 address, or an IPv6 address.
A device URI such as
.Li socket://192.168.0.80:9100
or a
.Li usb://
URI from
.Nm lpinfo Fl v
is used as given.
Before creating the queue,
.Nm
asks the printer which paper trays it has, over SNMP with
.Xr snmpwalk 1
or through the printer's web page with
.Xr curl 1 .
If the printer reports Tray 2, the queue is set up with both trays.
Jobs print from Tray 1 unless another tray is chosen.
.It Cm remove
Deletes a print queue that uses this driver.
Without a name it deletes
.Li Dell_Color_Laser_1320c .
Queues that use other drivers are never deleted.
.It Cm trays
Shows the paper trays the printer at
.Ar address
reports.
.It Cm list
Lists the print queues that use this driver, with their device URIs.
.It Cm refresh
Gives every print queue that uses this driver the installed PPD,
keeping the options chosen for each queue.
The installer packages run it after every install and upgrade.
.It Cm uninstall
Removes every print queue that uses this driver, then the driver itself.
Only available on macOS; on Linux, remove the driver with the package manager.
.It Cm version
Shows the driver version.
.El
.Pp
The options for
.Cm add
are:
.Bl -tag -width "--description text"
.It Fl \-name Ar name
Queue name.
The default is
.Li Dell_Color_Laser_1320c .
The name must not start with a hyphen or contain spaces,
.Sq / ,
.Sq # ,
.Sq \e ,
single quotes or double quotes.
.It Fl \-description Ar text
Name shown in print dialogs.
The default is
.Li Dell Color Laser 1320c .
.It Fl \-location Ar text
Location shown in print dialogs.
.It Fl \-paper Ar size
Default paper size, such as
.Li Letter
or
.Li A4 .
The default comes from the region set for the user running the command.
.It Fl \-protocol Cm lpd | socket
Protocol used when an address is given:
.Cm lpd ,
the default, or
.Cm socket ,
which prints to port 9100.
.It Fl \-default
Makes the queue the default printer.
.It Fl \-shared
Shares the queue on the network.
Queues are not shared by default.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "@PPD@"
.It Pa @PPD@
The driver's PPD.
.It Pa @DRIVER_DIR@
The driver's files, including the color correction tables.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create the default queue for a network printer and make it the default
printer:
.Dl sudo dell1320c add 192.168.0.80 \-\-default
.Pp
Create a queue for a USB printer with A4 paper:
.Dl sudo dell1320c add 'usb://Dell/Color%20Laser%201320c?serial=XXXXXXXX' \-\-paper A4
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lpoptions 1 ,
.Xr lpstat 1 ,
.Xr lpadmin 8 ,
.Xr lpinfo 8
